    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.03) anchoring the outfield as our clear priority starts. **Christian Yelich** benefits from a massive 13% platoon boost against McGreevy, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** thrives in a high-efficiency park environment, overcoming a sub-3.00 xERA matchup against Kremer. Both hitters are prioritized for their high-upside roles at the top of the order, where their elite sprint speed and base-stealing potential\u2014critical for our 5x5 Roto needs\u2014are maximized by high-volume plate appearances. Conversely, **Dillon Dingler** (63.90) and **Josh Smith** (62.54) also provide strong value, with both players seeing significant bumps from their #2 spots in the order and favorable platoon alignments against left- and right-handed arms, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Casey Schmitt** (43.52) and **Nelson Velazquez** (41.01). While both players cleared the Zebras\u2019 40.0 baseline, they were ultimately squeezed out by the depth of our middle infield and outfield rotations. **Casey Schmitt** suffered primarily from an elite-tier matchup against Cease, whose high-strikeout profile suppressed his efficiency score below the utility-grade floor required to displace **Kyle Schwarber** or **Caleb Durbin**. Meanwhile, **Nelson Velazquez** remains a high-variance play; his elite 0.420 xwOBA suggests he could easily outperform the projected total, but his matchup against Harrison (L) and a lower projected lineup slot forced the optimizer to favor the more stable floor of **Carson Benge**.\n\nRisk management remains a theme today, particularly with **Yordan Alvarez** (57.36) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (46.99). **Yordan Alvarez** is battling a significant platoon disadvantage against Griffin (L), which dampens his base projection, though his elite xwOBA keeps him in the starting lineup regardless. We are also monitoring the status of **Trea Turner**, who remains unavailable today; his absence continues to put pressure on our remaining roster to maintain speed volume. With no major weather concerns currently flagged, our focus remains on leveraging the platoon-heavy profiles of **Luke Raley** and **Junior Caminero** to stabilize the lineup against their respective right-handed opponents.",
